<title>FINLAND: Finland Bank adds EEK, KRW to currency index.</title>
<headline>Finland Bank adds EEK, KRW to currency index.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Finland said on Tuesday it was adding the Estonian kroon and the Republic of Korea won to its currency index.</p>
<p>&quot;After the change, the currency index includes 16 currencies and covers about 75 percent of Finland's foreign trade,&quot; the central bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>The index weight of the kroon is 2.6 percent and of the won 1.4 percent, the bank said, adding that from Tuesday it would include the won in its daily quotes of middle rates. It said trade between Finland and Estonia had grown rapidly recently.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +3589 6805 0247, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
